From: OneKVM Project <223006751+lowtech-guy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdc: copy wrap attributes before freeing the response

gdc_get_chn_buf_wrap writes its response into cfg.  Do not free cfg before
copying that response to the caller.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 modules/gdc/src/cvi_gdc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/gdc/src/cvi_gdc.c b/modules/gdc/src/cvi_gdc.c
index 790212a..e10ac39 100644
--- a/modules/gdc/src/cvi_gdc.c
+++ b/modules/gdc/src/cvi_gdc.c
@@ -348,11 +348,11 @@ CVI_S32 CVI_GDC_GetBufWrapAttr(GDC_HANDLE hHandle, const GDC_TASK_ATTR_S *pstTa
 
 	s32Ret = gdc_get_chn_buf_wrap(d->fd, cfg);
 
-	free(cfg);
-
 	if (s32Ret == CVI_SUCCESS)
 		memcpy(pstBufWrap, &cfg->stBufWrap, sizeof(*pstBufWrap));
 
+	free(cfg);
+
 	return s32Ret;
 }
 
-- 
2.50.1
